ja-writing-guard
Copyright (c) 2026 TakeshiTGAL. Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

This plugin follows the structure of two earlier Japanese "AI-writing"
skills and takes rule ideas from several other MIT-licensed projects. Phrase
lists and patterns were rewritten as Python regular expressions in rules.py;
the `source` field of each rule names the project it came from. The rewriting
instructions in rewrite.py and skills/rewrite-ja/SKILL.md follow the
principles of the first two projects below.

Predecessors whose structure this plugin imitates
-------------------------------------------------

yomiyasu
  https://github.com/nanaism/yomiyasu
  Copyright (c) 2026 nanaism
  MIT License
  Used: slop vocabulary, metaphor-verb and filler patterns, the em dash /
  trailing colon / bold / emoji checks and the same-ending-in-a-row check
  (scripts/yomiyasu_lint.py); the meaning-preservation rules (主張・比重・
  言い切りの強さ・文の働き, 足さない) and stance-based sentence endings (SKILL.md).

natural-japanese
  https://github.com/coji/natural-japanese
  Copyright (c) 2026 coji
  MIT License
  Used: forbidden-phrase and translationese catalogs, antithesis patterns and
  genre-specific thresholds (skills/natural-japanese/scripts/lint.py,
  references/forbidden-patterns.md, references/translationese.md); the
  "detection by machine, judgement by the writer" split and "do not apply a
  fix uniformly" (SKILL.md, references/revision-guide.md); the machine-score
  formula of references/diagnose.md is used by eval/run_eval.py to apply
  natural-japanese's own decision rule in the comparison.

Other projects rules were taken from
------------------------------------

textlint-rule-preset-ai-writing
  https://github.com/textlint-ja/textlint-rule-preset-ai-writing
  Copyright (c) 2025 azu — MIT License
  Used: bold-label list items, bold-only lines, info-prefix bold labels, hype
  expressions, 「まず最初に」, 「〜について解説します」.

textlint-rule-preset-ja-technical-writing (and the bundled
textlint-rule-ja-no-redundant-expression, textlint-rule-no-double-negative-ja)
  https://github.com/textlint-ja/textlint-rule-preset-ja-technical-writing
  Copyright (c) 2016 azu — MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2015 azu (textlint-rule-no-double-negative-ja) — MIT License
  Used: 「〜を行う」, 「〜ことができる」 for verbs other than する, double negatives.

textlint-rule-preset-JTF-style
  https://github.com/textlint-ja/textlint-rule-preset-JTF-style
  Copyright (c) 2015 azu — MIT License
  Used: half-width ! and ? inside Japanese text; dash checks.

patina
  https://github.com/devswha/patina
  Copyright (c) 2025 devswha; Copyright (c) devswha and patina contributors
  MIT License
  Used: chatbot residue, knowledge-cutoff disclaimers, false nuance, filler,
  empty optimism, throat-clearing, pseudo-insight, significance inflation,
  〜的 chains, -ing style add-ons, vague sources, stiff phrases, colon reveals,
  にとどまらず contrasts, leaked tool markup (oaicite, utm_source=chatgpt.com).

japanese-humanizer
  https://github.com/geonwoo-jeong/japanese-humanizer
  Copyright (c) 2026 日本語ヒューマナイザー管理者 — MIT License
  Used: masking quotes, code and URLs before matching (detector.py).

humanizer-ja
  https://github.com/gonta223/humanizer-ja
  Copyright (c) 2025 Siqi Chen (original: blader/humanizer)
  Copyright (c) 2026 SuguruKun_ai (Japanese version: humanizer-ja)
  MIT License
  Used: 「浮き彫りにしており」-style add-on phrases, empty optimism.

Humanizer JP
  https://github.com/matsutouya/humanizer-ja
  Copyright (c) 2026 paris0001 — MIT License
  Used: 「させていただきます」 repetition, preamble declarations.

Not used: matsuikentaro1/humanizer-japanese (no license file; read only for
the comparison table, no rules taken).

Evaluation data
---------------

eval/data/*/human/ holds excerpts of human-written Japanese under their own
terms, listed file by file in eval/data/README.md: Japanese government sites
under the Public Data License 1.0 (PDL1.0, compatible with CC BY 4.0) or the
Government Standard Terms of Use 2.0; Osaka City (CC BY 4.0 compatible terms);
Aozora Bunko works whose Japanese copyright term has expired; Diet records (Copyright Act art. 40(1));
Ruby reference manual (CC BY 3.0, rurema/doctree); cookpad/styleguide (CC BY
3.0); freee accessibility guidelines (CC BY 4.0); Sudachi documentation
(Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2017 Works Applications Co., Ltd.; text in
eval/data/LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt); Re:VIEW documentation (doc/* is MIT,
Copyright (c) 2006-2019 Minero Aoki, Kenshi Muto, Masayoshi Takahashi, Masanori
Kado; text in eval/data/LICENSES/Re-VIEW-doc-MIT.txt) and
textlint-rule-preset-ja-technical-writing (MIT, Copyright (c) 2016 azu).
Excerpts were trimmed (tags, navigation and footnote numbers removed). eval/data/*/ai*/ was written by an LLM for this project (MIT).

